---
import Layout from '../layouts/ProjectsPost.astro';
import { SITE_URL, PERSON_ID } from '../consts';

// References the Person node published on the homepage rather than
// duplicating it here.
const aboutPageLd = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'AboutPage',
	url: `${SITE_URL}/about`,
	name: 'About Me',
	mainEntity: { '@id': PERSON_ID },
};
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Vijendra Kumar (Vijevira) is a Senior Software Engineer at Apsona based in Bangalore, India, working on backend systems, AI, and payment infrastructure."
	pubDate={new Date('June 22 2025')}
	updatedDate={new Date('September 1 2026')}
	heroImage="/profile.png"
	avatarImage={true}
	structuredData={aboutPageLd}
>
	<p>
		Hi, I'm <strong>Vijendra Kumar</strong> — online you'll usually find me as <strong
			>Vijevira</strong
		>. I'm a Senior Software Engineer based in Bangalore, India, and this is the fuller story
		behind the projects and resume on this site.
	</p>

	<h3>Where I started</h3>
	<p>
		I grew up in Bihar and later moved to Bangalore, where I live and work today. I studied
		<strong>Computer Science and Engineering</strong> at the University Institute of Technology,
		The University of Burdwan, graduating with an <strong>8.38 CGPA</strong>. Before that, I
		scored <strong>84.2%</strong> in 12th grade at Delhi Public School, Varanasi, and a <strong
			>9.8 CGPA</strong
		> in 10th grade at Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalaya.
	</p>

	<h3>My work journey</h3>
	<p>
		My career began at <strong>Tata Consultancy Services (TCS)</strong> (Oct 2021 – Aug 2022),
		where I worked on frontend development — HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Angular, and Java — building
		reusable UI components and input validation systems for enterprise-scale web applications.
	</p>
	<p>
		I then joined <strong>Pratishthan Software Ventures</strong> (Sep 2022 – Aug 2024), engineering
		mission-critical payment infrastructure for banks: <strong>SEPA</strong> (Single Euro Payments
		Area), <strong>QCBIP</strong> (Qatar Central Bank Instant Payments), <strong>UAERT</strong>
		(UAE Real-Time Transfers), and <strong>SWIFT</strong> messaging flows. I built real-time
		payment flows, return/reject cycles, and SLA tracking mechanisms to meet strict regulatory
		standards, enhanced systems integrated with <strong>NACH</strong> and <strong>NPCI</strong>,
		and worked across the stack — securing API integrations, handling Kafka-based event streams,
		and ensuring compliance with <strong>ISO 20022</strong>.
	</p>
	<p>
		Today I'm a <strong>Senior Software Engineer at Apsona</strong>, where my work centers on
		<strong>backend engineering, AI systems, payment integrations, and system architecture</strong
		>. I built <strong>apsona_nexus_svc</strong>, a secure Node.js service that provides REST APIs
		to interact with <strong>HashiCorp Vault</strong> for credential management, led the
		org-wide <strong>clear cache system</strong>, designed the <strong
			>Merge button for Salesforce Lightning List View</strong
		>, built <strong>PDF storage uploads to client orgs</strong>, and helped split a legacy
		monorepo into scoped services like PDF SVC and SFDC SVC. Along the way I upgraded services from
		Node.js v8 to v18 and automated <strong>Excel merge operations via schedulers</strong>. The
		full year-by-year breakdown is on my <a href="/resume">resume</a>, and you can see this focus
		in practice on the <a href="/projects">projects</a> page.
	</p>
	<p>
		Alongside my full-time roles, I've also taken on freelance work as an <strong
			>AI Prompt Engineer at Alignerr</strong
		> and an <strong>AI Trainer at Outlier</strong>, exploring applied AI/ML through prompt
		refinement and model training on real-world data.
	</p>

	<h3>Tech stack &amp; skills</h3>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Languages:</strong> Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Node.js, Java, HTML, CSS</li>
		<li><strong>Frameworks:</strong> Angular, Loopback, Oe-Cloud, Node-RED</li>
		<li><strong>Databases:</strong> PostgreSQL</li>
		<li><strong>Dev Tools:</strong> Docker, Postman, RabbitMQ, GitHub</li>
		<li><strong>CS Fundamentals:</strong> Data Structures, Operating Systems, DBMS</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		I've solved <strong>350+ coding problems</strong>, maintain <strong
			>25+ public repositories on GitHub</strong
		>, and constantly experiment with open-source and side projects.
	</p>

	<h3>Certifications</h3>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>CutShort Certified</strong> – Python (Advanced) &amp; JavaScript (Advanced)</li>
		<li><strong>Udemy:</strong> Python (2019)</li>
		<li><strong>Coursera:</strong> Python Data Structures (2019), Algorithm Toolbox (2019)</li>
		<li><strong>edX:</strong> Object-Oriented Programming in Java (2019)</li>
		<li><strong>PM YUVA Yojana:</strong> Entrepreneurship (2018)</li>
		<li><strong>InfyTQ:</strong> Infosys Certified Software Programmer (2020)</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>Achievements</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>Global Rank <strong>690</strong> – <em>Facebook Hacker Cup</em></li>
		<li>Global Rank <strong>1899</strong> – <em>TCS CodeVita</em></li>
		<li>Round 3 – <em>CodeChef SnackDown</em></li>
	</ul>

	<h3>How I work</h3>
	<p>
		I care more about clean, thoughtful engineering than quick hacks — writing code that's easy for
		the next person (often future me) to reason about, testing it properly, and documenting
		decisions so they don't get lost. I like working with people who are equally curious, and I'm
		always looking for the next thing worth learning, whether that's a new part of the stack or an
		unfamiliar problem space like applied AI.
	</p>

	<h3>Outside of work</h3>
	<p>
		When I'm not writing code, I'm usually solving puzzles or playing chess — though most of that
		same energy ends up going into personal projects. I like building real-time multiplayer games
		on Cloudflare Workers and Durable Objects, complete with bot AI so they're playable solo: <a
			href="/projects/personal/cabo-card-game">Cabo</a
		> (2–15 players), <a href="/projects/personal/cuff-the-bluff">Cuff the Bluff</a> (a Liar's Dice
		game for up to 15 players), <a href="/projects/personal/splendor">Splendor</a> (a digital take
		on the board game for 2–12 players), and <a href="/projects/personal/chhakkadi-game"
			>Chhakkadi</a
		> (a platform for three Indian card games — Chhakkadi, Dehla Pakad, and Call Break).
	</p>
	<p>
		I've also built a couple of full SaaS products end-to-end: <a href="/projects/personal/zyvora"
			>Zyvora</a
		>, a Jira-like project management platform with Kanban boards and real-time collaboration, and
		<a href="/projects/personal/watchtower">WatchTower</a>, a platform that monitors websites, RSS
		feeds, and APIs and pushes notifications to Discord, Slack, and Telegram — plus smaller tools
		like a <a href="/projects/personal/notes-app">Notes App</a>. You can browse all of them on the
		<a href="/projects">projects</a> page.
	</p>

	<h3>Let's connect</h3>
	<p>
		I'm always open to interesting conversations, collaborations, or opportunities. You can reach
		me by email or find my other profiles in the footer below.
	</p>
</Layout>
